A cozy 1990s Swiss office training room rendered in Studio Ghibli style, warm afternoon light streaming through large windows onto wooden desks where diverse employees lean toward each other excitedly, passing handwritten paper sheets between desks like a chain reaction. Scattered croissant-shaped pastries on small plates, vintage beige computer monitors glowing softly, papers floating gently through the air between participants. The room buzzes with collaborative energy, people pointing at their sheets, some standing, creating an organic web of human connection. Soft watercolor textures, gentle shadows, whimsical details like steam rising from coffee cups, autumn trees visible outside. The atmosphere captures discovery and human problem-solving, a nostalgic warmth of people learning together before smartphones, the magic of genuine in-person collaboration emerging naturally.
